TSI SkyLP: ACPI description of the UDI subsystem
=================================================

skylp-udi.asl   SSDT for one SkyLP chiplet's UDI block: the udi_intr
                collector, the USB 3.2 DRD controller with the SkyLP init
                hooks, the Type-C lane-mux glue, the DP PHY, the DP TX
                controller and video bridge 0 (the DRM CRTC), including the
                _DSD graph link between bridge and DP controller.
enum-init.c     Static /init for a boot check: lists the platform devices
                the SSDT produced and powers off.

How the drivers find their description
--------------------------------------
Every device carries _HID "PRP0001" (or a TSI _HID with _CID "PRP0001") and
a _DSD "compatible" string identical to the devicetree binding. The kernel
matches the drivers' of_match_table through that string and serves the
_DSD properties through the same device_property_*() calls the drivers
already use, so devicetree and ACPI boards run the same driver code.

Three things have no ACPI equivalent of the DT phandle and are handled
explicitly:
  - interrupts from the UDI collector: an Extended Interrupt descriptor
    whose ResourceSource is the collector device; the number is the
    udi_intr bit. The collector's irq domain is keyed on its ACPI node.
  - the PHY and pixel clocks of the DP controller: the PHY's _DSD names
    the consumer device ("tsi,consumer") and the PHY driver registers
    phy/clk lookups under that name. The DP driver defers until they exist.
  - the CRTC-to-encoder link: the _DSD graph (port@0/endpoint@0 on both
    sides) is walked with fwnode_graph_*; the master fills in the
    encoder's possible_crtcs, which the vendor driver can only derive from
    an OF graph.

USB _CRS ordering (ACPI resources have no names): 0 controller, 1 lane
mux, 2 tsar_control, 3 udi_clk_sel.

Build and check
---------------
  iasl -oa -p skylp-udi skylp-udi.asl         -> skylp-udi.aml

Injecting the table before the BIOS carries it
----------------------------------------------
With CONFIG_ACPI_TABLE_UPGRADE the kernel takes SSDTs from an uncompressed
cpio at the start of the initrd:

  mkdir -p tbl/kernel/firmware/acpi
  cp skylp-udi.aml tbl/kernel/firmware/acpi/
  (cd tbl && find kernel | cpio -o -H newc) > tables.cpio
  cat tables.cpio initrd.img > initrd-with-tables.img

Boot with that initrd (and acpi=force on arm64 if a devicetree is also
present). "ACPI: table upgrade" lines in dmesg confirm the load.

QEMU enumeration check (no SkyLP hardware; drivers must not be built in,
since the register windows do not exist on the virt machine):

  aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc -static -Os -o init enum-init.c
  mkdir -p rootfs/sys rootfs/proc && cp init rootfs/init
  (cd rootfs && find . | cpio -o -H newc | gzip -9) > initrd.gz
  cat tables.cpio initrd.gz > initrd-with-tables.img
  qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a57 -m 1G -nographic \
    -drive if=pflash,format=raw,file=AAVMF_CODE.fd,readonly=on \
    -drive if=pflash,format=raw,file=AAVMF_VARS.fd \
    -kernel Image -initrd initrd-with-tables.img \
    -append "console=ttyAMA0 acpi=force"

Expected: one ENUM line per device with modalias
"acpi:PRP0001:" / "acpi:TSI0000x:PRP0001:" and the _DSD compatible in the
of: alias, and the ACPI path under \_SB.LP0.

Open items encoded as comments in the ASL
-----------------------------------------
  - tsi,tsar-init / tsi,clksel-init values (HW-8, HW-4 bit maps)
  - plug-event / plug-flip GPIOs need the SkyLP GPIO controller in ACPI
  - LP1 (the chiplet behind the J43 DP receptacle on Helix-M) needs its
    own copy of the block with its base addresses and rollup (HW-35)
